AB  - In support of the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs), particularly the goal of “Industry, Innovation and Infrastructure,” AR/VR immersive technologies are increasingly important for industrial innovation and intelligent infrastructure, yet they face challenges in balancing real-time adaptive generation with high visual quality. This paper investigates real-time adaptation and interactive design of generative visual content for AR/VR experiences, proposing an integrated framework combining Multi-Modal Conditional GANs, Information Maximizing VAEs, multi-task deep reinforcement learning, and GAN-DRL joint optimization. Experimental results demonstrate significant improvements in generation quality, efficiency, adaptability, and diversity, enabling high-quality, real-time intelligent content generation. The proposed approach overcomes key limitations of traditional methods and provides a robust technical paradigm for intelligent AR/VR infrastructure, contributing to the advancement of the SDGs’ “Industry, Innovation and Infrastructure” objective and the digital creative industry.
