AB  - Sixth-generation wireless networks are required to enable real-time holographic communication as well as augmented reality and virtual reality applications. This enables ultra-high data rates and sub-millisecond latency. These applications generate massive volumes of volumetric and high-resolution 3D data with multi-view. Conventional codecs like H.265/HEVC introduce computational delay though it provides high compression efficiency. Superior quality can be provided through deep learningbased compression techniques but they fail to satisfy latency constraints. This work presents a hybrid compression method combining H.265/HEVC baseline encoding with Generative Adversarial Network. These are kept at edge computing nodes. Evaluation results indicate enhanced compression ratio, decreased bit error rate, and reduced latency. Further, this technique is compared to standalone traditional and AI-based methods. This proposed study is applicable for real-time holographic and sixth generation communication systems.
ER  - 

