AB  - Social interaction is a fundamental part of daily life, but for individuals with autism, it can be difficult and stressful. This paper introduces EchoMind, a virtual reality (VR) training system that helps users build social communication skills through immersive, voice-based role-play. EchoMind combines speech recognition, generative AI, and real-time dialogue with a virtual agent named Allen, who is designed to be patient, supportive, and emotionally supportive. The system provides structured prompts developed by educators, covering scenarios such as school conversations and workplace interactions. By enabling natural, guided conversations in a safe environment, EchoMind aims to enhance user confidence, alleviate anxiety, and foster long-term social development.
ER  - 

