AB  - This study presents an LLM-based augmented reality (AR) system designed to enhance cultural heritage exploration through natural language question answering (QA) and quiz-based interactions. A structured knowledge base guides the LLM to provide context-aware explanations in response to user queries, while generated quiz items transform cultural heritage data into interactive learning content within an AR environment. The system supports in-situ and map-based exploration, enabling users to review and learn from questions generated by others, fostering collective knowledge building. This design demonstrates the potential of combining LLM-driven interaction with AR to enrich interpretation, support learning, and promote cultural heritage experiences.
