AB  - Most mixed reality (MR) guidance systems rely on static instructions, overlooking user behavioral and cognitive variability. We present a multimodal adaptive guidance framework that combines LLM-generated task graphs with semantic step tracking driven by multimodal interaction events. The system also continuously logs gaze, hand, and head signals to support future temporal user state modeling. In an example MR guidance task, the system achieves robust step tracking with real-time responsiveness ($\approx 60 \text{ms}$ action-to-classification latency). Together, these results demonstrate reliable task progress monitoring and establish a foundation for user state-aware adaptive MR guidance.
ER  - 

