AB  - Presenting information in Mixed Reality is essential for immersive applications, yet current systems largely depend on static 3D layouts or manual placement, which limits adaptability across diverse environmental contexts. We introduce SpatiaLLM, a multi-agent framework leveraging Large Language Models (LLMs) to place adaptive, scene-aware MR content. SpatiaLLM grounds LLM intent reasoning in a constraint-verified spatial memory (ST-CM) that enforces physical feasibility (support contact, collision avoidance, free space) and scene continuity via constrained re-generation. Across three real-world indoor environments, average placement error drops from 65.2 % (single-prompt baseline) to 8.6 %. A user study ($\mathrm{n}=11$) reports improved coherence, stability, and adaptability.
ER  - 

