AB  - This paper demonstrates how Generative AI serves as a crucial element which drives the complete transformation of Virtual Reality (VR) and Augmented Reality (AR) systems. The implementation of advanced machine learning models enables these immersive technologies to deliver authentic dynamic content which matches individual user preferences. The research demonstrates how Generative AI enables users to design complex virtual environments which include dynamic educational materials and user interfaces that boost user interaction in gaming educational and professional development environments. The research investigates how AI technology combines haptic feedback systems and neural interfaces to create deeper user immersion experiences through better interactive capabilities. The paper discusses essential ethical issues and practical matters which include privacy rights and AI-generated content effects on actual life situations and virtual environment extended usage consequences on mental health. The discussions establish a requirement for comprehensive regulatory systems which include ethical standards to guarantee responsible technology utilization. The paper demonstrates that research and development need to continue because it studies current trends and future projections which show how Generative AI should be used in virtual reality and augmented reality technology according to ethical standards. The study recommends two different approaches which organizations should use to develop their technologies through partnerships which will enable them to achieve their development goals in a responsible manner.
