AB  - This paper introduces an Augmented Reality based feedback system for speech therapy and language learning. It aims to overcome common challenges in speech therapy such as lack of motivation, and a struggle to bring the clinical skills to real life situations - called the "carryover" problem. Traditional speech therapy involves repeated exercises that can cause burnout and becomes less interesting for users. Our system aims to bring Generative AI to an interactive AR interface for a more interactive, randomised, and dynamic way to make the process of practicing more engaging. The platform uses several AI models: GPT-2 for generating new practice sentences for user to read, Wav2Vec2.0 for transcribing user speech, a BERT-based Sentence Transformer for assessing pronunciation through semantic similarity, and VITS for producing audio of correct pronunciation for reference. This smart feedback loop is integrated to an AR-web frontend using A-Frame and AR.js. This paper demonstrates the system architecture, process, and how it can be used as an effective complementary tool for therapists and an interactive learning platform for students. The aim is to fill the gaps in motivation and real-world "carryover" of speaking skills.
ER  - 

